WEBVTT

00:00:00.015 --> 00:00:02.549
Easy Fables. Part 3.

00:00:02.549 --> 00:00:05.146
The Town Mouse and the Country Mouse.

00:00:05.146 --> 00:00:08.444
A town mouse went to visit his friend in the country.

00:00:08.444 --> 00:00:11.580
The country mouse gave him the best food he had.

00:00:11.580 --> 00:00:14.650
It was only some dry bread and a few beans.

00:00:14.650 --> 00:00:18.101
"How can you live like this?" said the town mouse.

00:00:18.101 --> 00:00:19.926
"Come to the town with me.

00:00:19.926 --> 00:00:21.891
There you can eat like a king."

00:00:21.891 --> 00:00:24.354
So the two friends went to the town.

00:00:24.354 --> 00:00:29.496
In a big house they found a table covered with cake, cheese and fruit.

00:00:29.496 --> 00:00:30.874
They began to eat.

00:00:30.874 --> 00:00:34.050
But then the door opened and a big cat ran in.

00:00:34.050 --> 00:00:38.013
The mice ran for their lives and hid in a hole in the wall.

00:00:38.013 --> 00:00:42.856
"I am going home," said the country mouse, when the cat had gone.

00:00:42.856 --> 00:00:47.107
"My food is simple, but I can eat it without being afraid."

00:00:47.107 --> 00:00:51.493
A simple life in peace is better than a rich life full of fear.

00:00:51.493 --> 00:00:53.757
The Wolf in Sheep's Clothing.

00:00:53.757 --> 00:00:58.805
A wolf wanted to eat the sheep, but the farmer watched them too carefully.

00:00:58.805 --> 00:01:02.672
One day the wolf found the skin of a sheep on the ground.

00:01:02.672 --> 00:01:05.328
He put it on and walked into the field.

00:01:05.328 --> 00:01:07.504
Now he looked just like a sheep.

00:01:07.504 --> 00:01:09.949
The other sheep were not afraid of him.

00:01:09.949 --> 00:01:14.818
They let him walk with them, and the farmer did not see anything strange.

00:01:14.818 --> 00:01:20.627
That evening the farmer shut all the sheep in for the night, and the wolf was shut in with them.

00:01:20.627 --> 00:01:23.755
Later, the farmer wanted some meat for dinner.

00:01:23.755 --> 00:01:29.143
He went out in the dark, took the first animal he found, and killed it.

00:01:29.143 --> 00:01:30.506
It was the wolf.

00:01:30.506 --> 00:01:33.841
Those who try to hurt others often hurt themselves.

00:01:33.841 --> 00:01:35.690
The Two Friends and the Bear.

00:01:35.690 --> 00:01:38.351
Two friends were walking through a forest.

00:01:38.351 --> 00:01:41.459
Suddenly a big bear came out from the trees.

00:01:41.459 --> 00:01:45.888
One of the men ran to a tree and climbed up as fast as he could.

00:01:45.888 --> 00:01:48.450
He did not think about his friend at all.

00:01:48.450 --> 00:01:50.577
The other man could not climb.

00:01:50.577 --> 00:01:53.392
He lay down on the ground and did not move.

00:01:53.392 --> 00:01:56.675
He had heard that bears do not touch dead things.

00:01:56.675 --> 00:02:00.515
The bear came up to him and put its nose near his ear.

00:02:00.515 --> 00:02:02.400
The man held his breath.

00:02:02.400 --> 00:02:04.596
At last the bear walked away.

00:02:04.596 --> 00:02:07.083
The first man came down from the tree.

00:02:07.083 --> 00:02:11.476
"What did the bear say in your ear?" he asked, laughing.

00:02:11.476 --> 00:02:17.910
"He told me," said his friend, "never to travel with a man who runs away when there is danger."

00:02:17.910 --> 00:02:20.975
A real friend stays with you in hard times.

00:02:20.975 --> 00:02:22.963
The Farmer and His Sons.

00:02:22.963 --> 00:02:25.366
An old farmer was very sick.

00:02:25.366 --> 00:02:27.344
He knew he would die soon.

00:02:27.344 --> 00:02:29.928
He called his three sons to his bed.

00:02:29.928 --> 00:02:35.341
"My sons," he said, "there is something valuable hidden in our fields.

00:02:35.341 --> 00:02:37.567
Dig, and you will find it."

00:02:37.567 --> 00:02:42.551
After the old man died, the sons took their tools and began to dig.

00:02:42.551 --> 00:02:45.182
They dug up every part of every field.

00:02:45.182 --> 00:02:47.744
They found no gold and no silver.

00:02:47.744 --> 00:02:49.332
They were very sad.

00:02:49.332 --> 00:02:52.210
But the ground had never been dug so well.

00:02:52.210 --> 00:02:57.798
That year the fields gave more food than ever before, and the sons became rich.

00:02:57.798 --> 00:03:01.345
Then they understood what their father had wanted to tell them.

00:03:01.345 --> 00:03:03.566
Hard work is the real gold.

00:03:03.566 --> 00:03:05.607
The Milk Girl and Her Pail.

00:03:05.607 --> 00:03:09.932
A girl was walking to the market with a pail of milk on her head.

00:03:09.932 --> 00:03:13.032
As she walked, she began to make plans.

00:03:13.632 --> 00:03:17.598
"I will sell this milk and buy some eggs," she thought.

00:03:17.598 --> 00:03:19.831
"The eggs will become chickens.

00:03:19.831 --> 00:03:23.037
I will sell the chickens and buy a beautiful dress.

00:03:23.037 --> 00:03:27.021
At the dance, all the young men will want to talk to me.

00:03:27.021 --> 00:03:30.077
But I will just shake my head, like this."

00:03:30.077 --> 00:03:31.484
She shook her head.

00:03:31.484 --> 00:03:35.841
The pail fell off, and all the milk ran out onto the road.

00:03:35.841 --> 00:03:39.916
She had nothing to sell, and she went home with nothing.

00:03:39.916 --> 00:03:43.723
Do not count your chickens before they come out of their eggs.
